{
	"_about": "Food and drink. Eat the one in hand with the food slot (key 7, Q = next food); the seed stand sells the ones with shop true. Per food: name, price (G at the stand), stamina (+, up to the max), fatigue (+ or -, mostly -), drink (true = drunk, uses the drink sound), and optional specials: max_stamina (raises the max, up to max_stamina_cap) and work_fatigue_half (fatigue from tool swings is halved until the day ends), with special_message. look draws the placeholder icon (shape: rice_ball, round, skewer, cup, bottle, bowl, plate, fish_plate, bag, imo; colors; top and marks: the dish's own detail as drawing steps [\"px\", x, y, w, h, colour], [\"oval\", cx, cy, rx, ry, colour], [\"line\", x0, y0, x1, y1, colour], [\"dots\", colour, x, y, ...] on the 14 x 14 icon, top toned like the rest, marks kept in their colours; bare true skips the shape and draws the top alone; steam: columns of steam over a hot bowl; see PlaceholderArt.food_layers). Foods of one shape differ by more than colour (test_menu). Dishes with shop false come from the kitchen (data/recipes.json); foods with shop false and a price (yakisoba, shaved ice, marble soda, roast chestnuts, baked sweet potato, year-end soba, hot yuzu tea) are sold only at a festival stall (data/festivals.json); the herb tonic (price 0 here, 400 G in data/shops.json) only at the clinic. Fumi's teahouse sweets and whipped matcha (shop false, with a price) are sold only at the Hanami teahouse (data/shops.json teahouse). sell: what one fetches in the shipping bin (dishes only; held out at the bin or thrown in, never taken from the rucksack by the bin), set at about 1.3 x the shipping value of ordinary ingredients (the cheapest crop of a group, eggs and milk at the middle grade, a fish at about 60 G), per dish. raw: farm goods (and wild berries and akebi from data/forage.json) eaten as they are (from the rucksack with the eat key, or held overhead with the food slot in hand), keyed by item id, fish:* for any fish; stamina, fatigue, drink as above. A food that would do nothing (stamina full, no fatigue, no special) is not eaten. pose: seconds the farmer stands eating (eat) or drinking (drink) after anything is eaten, unable to move or act (about two bites / one long sip; FarmerAnim sets the frame rate). Names and numbers are ours; see WORKLOG 2026-10-31 Eating and Cooking.",
	"_dish_prices": "A cooked dish sells for about a third more than its cheapest ingredients shipped raw (plain eggs and milk, the cheapest fish: dace or loach at 18 G), so cooking to sell is a modest gain and never a shortcut; a better grade or a dearer fish is worth more raw. Grilled fish was 80 G for one fish (FEEDBACK item 5, WORKLOG 2026-11-04); `python -I tools/balance.py` prints every recipe's gain (its last table, column cheap). Stamina is what a dish is really for.",
	"max_stamina_cap": 200,
